# ref-16f7f4c-mesh-dense-contact
# A box dropped onto a dense triangle mesh patch, 100 steps at fixed dt=1/60,
# 4 substeps, no wall clock.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 16f7f4c.
# Fixed: fixed3d on this branch. The mesh-contact triangle-index and contact-cache
#   scratch is allocated from the per-worker arena, sized by the cap
#   (B3_MAX_MESH_CONTACT_TRIANGLES, 512, still a public #ifndef tunable).
# Observable: contact count and resting height of the dropped box after 100 steps.
# Tolerance: NOT MEASURED. The reference harness (tools/reference/, card
#   fixed3d-box3d-reference-harness) is absent at BASE sprint/fixed3d-box3d-ports
#   (1df2e22): this tree has scenes only, and no ctest -L reference target.
#   Do not treat the numbers below as a measured band. When the harness lands,
#   set the resting-height band to twice the measured maximum absolute error
#   and require contact counts to match, and say why in the port record.
#   Never loosen a measured band to pass.
# Fixed-point divergence (by design, CLAUDE.md): the engine is Q48.16 with the
#   exact-SAT structure and no float SIMD hull core, so transform traces are not
#   bit-identical to float. The box must still come to rest on the mesh.
scene ref-16f7f4c-mesh-dense-contact
mesh wave 40 40 cell 1.0 amplitude 0.5 rowHz 0.1 columnHz 0.2
body box half 0.5 position 0 5 0 density 1.0
steps 100 dt 1/60 substeps 4
expect contactCount >= 1
expect restingY > -2.0
